    return (10 - (sum % 10)) % 10;
}
```

---

## 3. Region-and-hash identity key (SHA-256, full — distinct from HASH8)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/IdentityKey.java`** — note this is a *separate* full-64-char SHA-256 hex used for duplicate rejection (not the customerCode HASH8).
- L43-47 `of(Owner)` = `sha256Hex(normalizedTelephone + "|" + lowerEmail + "|" + Soundex.of(lastName))`.
- L49-61 `sha256Hex(String)` (full lower-case hex).
- L63-74 `rejectIfDuplicate(Owner, Collection<Owner>)` — throws `DuplicateTelephoneException(key)` on a full identity-key match (skips soft-deleted). This is the hard-duplicate/collision rejection path:
```java
public static void rejectIfDuplicate(Owner candidate, Collection<Owner> existingOwners) {
    String key = of(candidate);
    for (Owner owner : existingOwners) {
        if (owner.isDeleted()) {
            continue;
        }
        if (key.equals(of(owner))) {
            throw new DuplicateTelephoneException(key);
        }
    }
}
```
- L77-79 `telephone(...)` (digits only), L82-84 `email(...)` (lower/trim).
- Call site: `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` L125 `IdentityKey.rejectIfDuplicate(owner, ...)`.

Related soft-duplicate logic: **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/PossibleDuplicate.java`** — L22-26 `assign(...)`, L28-40 `matchId(...)` (matches soundex(lastName)+postcode but differing identity key). Call site L129.

---

## 4. Fiscal year

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/FiscalYear.java`** — FY starts 1 July.
- L16-18 `of(LocalDate)`:
```java
public static int of(LocalDate date) {
    return date.getMonthValue() >= 7 ? date.getYear() : date.getYear() - 1;
}
```
- L21-23 `label(LocalDate)` → `"FY%02d"` of `floorMod(of(date),100)`.

Used in: `OwnerMapper` L26 (`fiscalYear` label) and L27 (`membershipNumber` `-M<YY>`); `Membership.points` L31 (tenure spanning >1 elapsed fiscal year → +3 points).

---

## 5. Membership points / level

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/Membership.java`**
- L20-35 `points(Owner)`: +2 email present, +1 no namesakes, +2 household gold, +3 when `FiscalYear.of(now) - FiscalYear.of(registrationDate) > 1`.
- L38-49 `level(int points)`: 4 (≥6), 3 (≥4), 2 (≥2), else 1.

Level ceiling: **`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/LevelCeiling.java`** L23-34 `cap(int level, Owner, Collection<Owner>)` caps to one above max household member level. Call site: `OwnerRestControllerV1` L132.

Supporting: **`GoldTier.java`** L19-24 `qualifies(...)` (household ≥3 → gold); **`Household.java`** L22-35 `idFor(Owner)` = 12 upper-hex of SHA-256 over `normalizedLastName + "|" + postcode`; **`Namesakes.java`** L16-25 `count(...)`.

---

## 6. Owner segment

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/OwnerSegment.java`**
- L13 `METRO_REGIONS = Set.of("NSW", "VIC", "QLD")`.
- L19-23 `of(int membershipLevel, String locality)`:
```java
public static String of(int membershipLevel, String locality) {
    String tier = membershipLevel >= 3 ? "PREMIUM" : "STANDARD";
    String area = METRO_REGIONS.contains(locality) ? "METRO" : "REGIONAL";
    return tier + "_" + area;
}
```
Wired at `OwnerMapper` L37.

---

## 7. Audit record logic

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/util/OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** — the structured `OWNER_CREATED` event to the `AUDIT` logger.
- L19 `AtomicLong SEQ`.
- L25-27 `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` returns `owner.getCustomerCode()` (javadoc L14-16 notes the future `memberId`).
- L30-34 `emit(Owner, Object membershipLevel)`:
```java
public static void emit(Owner owner, Object membershipLevel) {
    LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT").info(
        "{\"seq\":{},\"ownerId\":{},\"customerCode\":\"{}\",\"membershipLevel\":\"{}\",\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}",
        SEQ.incrementAndGet(), owner.getId(), primaryIdentifier(owner), membershipLevel);
}
```

**Second audit sink (inline in the controller) — `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**
- L133: a second `AUDIT` log line (human-readable) including `customerCode`, `registrationDate`, `membershipLevel`, `membershipNumber`:
```java
org.slf4j.LoggerFactory.getLogger("AUDIT").info("owner id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={} membershipLevel={} membershipNumber={}", owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate(), ownerDto.getMembershipLevel(), ownerDto.getMembershipNumber());
```
- L134: `OwnerCreatedEvent.emit(owner, ownerDto.getMembershipLevel());`

---

## 8. OpenAPI schema definitions (source of the generated `OwnerDto`)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** — field schemas (the DTO is generated from these):
- L2164-2171 `customerCode` (STALE doc: still `<LAST3>-<NNNN>`, `SMI-0007`)
- L2172-2179 `householdId` (doc mentions "collision"-adjacent: same last name/address)
- L2190-2198 `fiscalYear` (`FY<YY>`)
- L2199-2206 `membershipNumber` (`<customerCode>-M<YY>`)
- L2207-2217 `membershipPoints`; L2218-2228 `membershipLevel`
- L2229-2236 `locality`; L2237-2245 `timezone`
- L2281-2289 `identityKey`; L2290-2300 `checkDigit` (Luhn over customerCode digits)
- L2328-2336 `ownerSegment` (`<TIER>_<AREA>`)
- L2061-2062 region/postcode ranges (in postcode field description)

Note the discrepancy: `customerCode` (L2167) and `membershipNumber` (L2202) descriptions and examples describe the old sequence-based scheme, but `CustomerCode.java` implements `<REGION>-<HASH8>`. Likewise `identityKey` doc (L2284) says `...|householdId` whereas `IdentityKey.of` actually uses `soundex(lastName)`.

---

## 9. Test files referencing these fields

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceTest.java`**
- L7-9 javadoc: states the *target* unification — `customerCode` + `membershipNumber` unified into `memberId = '<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>'`.
- L13-20 `coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId()`: computes `hash8 = shaHex(telephone + lastName, 8)`, asserts `memberId` starts with `NSW`, contains `hash8`, and that `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` are gone. (This asserts a future/desired state; current API still returns the old fields.)

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AcceptanceBase.java`** — the test harness with reference algorithms:
- L228-229 `CITY_REGION`; L232-233 `REGION_TIMEZONE`; L236-237 `REGION_POSTCODES`; L240-242 `HOLIDAYS`.
- L244-246 `region(city)`; L248-250 `timezone(city)`; L252-256 `validPostcode(city)`; L260-265 `knownOwner(city)`.
- L282-294 `sha256hex(String)` (full lower-hex SHA-256); L297-299 `shaHex(String, int)` (first n UPPER-case hex = HASH8 helper); L302-321 `luhn(String)` (reference Luhn implementation matching `CheckDigit.luhn`).

**`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/test/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/acceptance/AuditLogCapture.java`** — Logback `ListAppender` capturing the `AUDIT` logger (L31-33 default logger name `"AUDIT"`), with `messages()`, `anyContains(...)`, `anyAtLevel(...)`, `count()` for asserting audit side-effects.

---

## Notes / observations
- The literal string "collision" does not appear anywhere in the codebase; collision handling is realized as (a) hard-duplicate rejection in `IdentityKey.rejectIfDuplicate`, and (b) uniqueness suffixing in `UniqueCustomerCode.assign` (`isTaken` loop).
- `memberId` exists only as a concept: referenced in `OwnerCreatedEvent` javadoc (L15) as a future replacement and asserted by `AcceptanceTest` (L16-19). No production field/getter named `memberId` exists yet.
- Two SHA-256 usages differ: `CustomerCode.hash8` (4 bytes → 8 UPPER hex, HASH8) and `Household.idFor` (6 bytes → 12 UPPER hex) both use `%02X`; `IdentityKey.sha256Hex` produces full 64-char lower hex (`%02x`).

